  This function brings the specified window to front and sets input focus. The window should already be visible and not iconified. By default, both windowed and full screen mode windows are focused when initially created. Set the GLFW_FOCUSED to disable this behavior. Also by default, windowed mode windows are focused when shown with glfwShowWindow. Set the GLFW_FOCUS_ON_SHOW to disable this behavior. __Do not use this function__ to steal focus from other applications unless you are certain that is what the user wants. Focus stealing can be extremely disruptive. For a less disruptive way of getting the user's attention, see attention requests.

  Args:
    window: The window to give input focus.

  Errors:
    Possible errors include GLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED and GLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR.

  Note:
